Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Do you want a well-paid side job as a Warehouse Employee near Nijmegen, in the evenings during the week or in the weekend? You start at €15.69 gross per hour, and with the weekend rates you can earn up to €23.50 per hour. As a Warehouse Employee you:  - Take stock of the products in the warehouse;
 - Check and process new and incoming products;
 - Get orders ready for shipment.


What makes this job stand out is the flexibility. Your working days are set in consultation, and there is understanding for things that take up your time, such as an exam week.

From a Warehouse Employee, we expect the following:  - You're available on short notice, preferably right away;
 - You have your own transport to get to Oosterhout (near Nijmegen);
 - A proficiency in English and/or Dutch on B1/B2 level.

 In this role it's important that you're a detail orientated person, accuracy is more important than speed in this position.

As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse operation. Together with your colleagues, you make sure orders are processed efficiently and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Operating an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Loading and unloading goods;
- Checking products for accuracy and completeness;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workplace.

Thanks to a structured onboarding program, you'll quickly learn all aspects of the job.

- Are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Have a basic understanding of Dutch and/or English;
- Enjoy physical and active work;
- Work accurately and responsibly;
- Are motivated and eager to learn.

Previous logistics experience is a plus, but not required.
